+`native_selection` is a closed choice: **`paired` (default)** or `normal-only`.
+Omitting the input preserves the paired A-then-B chain. `normal-only` is accepted
+only with `verification_scope=native-evidence`; other combinations and unknown
+values fail before native allocation. Preflight remains nonbuilding and always
+binds **both** manifests; normal-only still requires both reviewed control hashes.
+
+The coordinator may select `normal-only` only after independent review of actual
+A evidence establishes the precise reusable scope and a B-only continuation is
+justified. It still needs reviewed source/control commits, regenerated committed
+inventory and a fresh same-source preflight. Earlier A results remain at their
+original SHA: this input neither certifies reuse nor upgrades strict failures.
+Normal-only uses the unchanged B runner/budgets/lifecycle, allocates or claims no
+A lane, and cannot delete an unselected A evidence directory. Selection is bound
+into continuation state and cleanup receipts. Success is `NORMAL_ONLY_PASS`,
+never combined `PASS`; an ordinary failing result is `NORMAL_ONLY_NOT_READY`.
+Exceptions remain `FAIL`. No A receipt is synthesized, and final full qualification
+is still separate. Never use selection to bypass an unsafe paired A finalizer.
+
 The adapter uses only read-only Actions API requests. It verifies the exact
 producer repository, branch, source, workflow, attempt, successful result,
 artifact identity/digest and four bounded nonsymlink ZIP members before writing
 anything from the archive. It installs the binding byte-for-byte at the same
 absolute checkout path and recomputes both control manifests before native work.
 
